      "value": "A powerful portrayal of Jeffrey Sachs's ambitious quest to end global poverty. As  Secretary General of the United Nations and author of Fools Rush In Sachs argues that extreme poverty is a solvable problem, drawing on success stories from his daring five-year Millennium Villages Project experiment in Africa to demonstrate how specific initiatives can enable profound positive changes."
